RESPONSE: We still have the stray broken word and tab in the wrong spot.  Rather than clicking pixel‐perfectly, let’s use keyboard navigation: jump to the start of the line, move past three words, then insert the tab.

```python
import pyautogui, time

# 1) Make sure we’re at the start of the first paragraph
pyautogui.click(x=400, y=470)   # focus into the first line
time.sleep(0.2)
pyautogui.hotkey('home')        # go to beginning of line
time.sleep(0.2)

# 2) Jump three words forward
for _ in range(3):
    pyautogui.hotkey('ctrl', 'right')
    time.sleep(0.2)

# 3) Insert the tab at that spot
pyautogui.press('tab')
```

